DESCRIPTION >
    Daily FX rates, same shape as Merton fx_rates (ADR-VAL-06): one base_currency is worth rate units of
    quote_currency. USD/THB and THB/USD are different pairs; inverse handling stays in Merton.
    Primary source: EODHD /api/eod/{BASE}{QUOTE}.FOREX (rate = close).
    Fallback: Yahoo chart API {BASE}{QUOTE}=X (close rounded to priceHint).
    Market rates, not official reference rates.
    Highest version wins per (base_currency, quote_currency, rate_date); query with FINAL.
    Same key from both sources: EODHD always wins over Yahoo; within a source the latest fetch wins
    (version = source rank x 10^13 + ingest epoch ms; EODHD rank 2, YAHOO rank 1).

SCHEMA >
    `base_currency` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.base_currency`,
    `quote_currency` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.quote_currency`,
    `rate_date` Date32 `json:$.rate_date`,
    `rate` Decimal(23, 8) `json:$.rate`,
    `source` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.source`,
    `ingested_at` DateTime64(3) `json:$.ingested_at`,
    `version` UInt64 `json:$.version`

ENGINE "ReplacingMergeTree"
ENGINE_VER version
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "base_currency, quote_currency, rate_date"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toYear(rate_date)"

TOKEN ingest_token APPEND
